      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "When our system was not working properly after only four years we contacted My Solar who passed us onto Chromagen who eventually sent someone out to replace the inverter. However as no one was sent to actually check the system, the inverter, which cost US $150 in labour to replace, was not the problem so I contacted a local solar expert, Solargain, if anyone wants to get a solar power system, who took less than five minutes to find that a bank of eight panels were not working, and within an hour had it repaired. At a cost, again to US of $165. Now I am trying to get some of that back from Chromagen but they don't even have the courtesy to reply to my emails and phone calls. But they were quick to organise a quote for a new system.They won't even publish this response.",
